1
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:18,840
♪ I notice every glance ♪

2
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:23,680
♪ The way you look at me ♪

3
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:29,120
♪ And what they're hiding inside ♪

4
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:32,960
♪ I think we might be the same ♪

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,200
♪ Hiding our true feelings ♪

6
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,000
♪ Not wanting them to come out ♪

7
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,680
♪ But the closer we get ♪

8
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:47,520
♪ The more my heart wavers ♪

9
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:52,120
♪ I want to surrender to every voice in my heart ♪

10
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:54,520
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

11
00:00:54,520 --> 00:00:58,000
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

12
00:00:58,320 --> 00:00:59,600
How shameless.

13
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:01,480
Only 119 days left.

14
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,080
I guess I'll endure it.

15
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:04,400
Do whatever you want.

16
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:08,840
Please get out of my room.

17
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:10,480
You're quick to throw me out.

18
00:01:10,480 --> 00:01:11,800
If it were Smith...

19
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,760
So you really don't want me anymore?

20
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:19,000
CONSIDER THIS YOUR FEE

21
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,159
ONG

22
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,160
Hey, Ong.

23
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:01,160
Oh!

24
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,480
Mom had a fever this evening.

25
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:03,960
I gave her medicine

26
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:05,360
and wiped her down,

27
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:07,200
the fever just wouldn't go down

28
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,480
It was almost 40 degrees.

29
00:06:09,680 --> 00:06:11,400
I've brought her to the hospital now,

30
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:12,800
and the doctor wants to admit her.

31
00:06:13,200 --> 00:06:14,360
How did Mom get sick?

32
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,320
She probably

33
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:17,640
got caught in the rain

34
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,120
when she was helping me bring in the laundry.

35
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:22,240
Oh, I'm sorry.

36
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,200
I couldn't stop her in time.

37
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:26,160
It's okay, Ong. It's okay.

38
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,920
Oh,

39
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:30,160
do you have any money?

40
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,600
What you gave me

41
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,760
might not be enough.

42
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:46,920
I do,

43
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,640
but it's in cash.

44
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:52,760
I'll take care of it.

45
00:06:53,840 --> 00:06:54,840
Okay.

46
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:56,600
Go look after Mom.

47
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,320
Keep me updated on what the doctor says.

48
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:00,520
Yes.

49
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,640
Bua, if you're done, you can go rest.

50
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:30,640
Got it.

51
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:35,960
Cream,

52
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:37,240
are you free?

53
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:39,000
I need to talk to you about something.

54
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,400
Yeah,

55
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,040
sure.

56
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:45,159
I need to transfer some money

57
00:07:45,159 --> 00:07:46,320
to my sister urgently.

58
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:48,480
May I have permission to leave?

59
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:49,600
Go out at this hour?

60
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,040
It's late, Oh.

61
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,960
Want me to wire it for you?

62
00:07:56,240 --> 00:07:57,320
What do you say?

63
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,800
Yeah,

64
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:02,680
sorry to trouble you.

65
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:04,200
Here's 30,000 baht.

66
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,400
Count it first.

67
00:08:05,920 --> 00:08:06,920
Wow,

68
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:09,680
why are you carrying so much cash?

69
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,600
Send me the account number.

70
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:30,720
Okay, done.

71
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,680
Thanks.

72
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,240
Hey, Cream,

73
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:44,080
is Ms. Song staying here tonight?

74
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:46,080
Probably.

75
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,840
I saw her working in her study.

76
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:49,840
Is something up?

77
00:08:50,880 --> 00:08:51,920
Nothing.

78
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,360
Thanks.

79
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,640
What is this?

80
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:08,360
It's paper.

81
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:09,960
Don't you know what it is?

82
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:12,240
What does it mean?

83
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,400
It means what it says.

84
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:19,400
Then what happened earlier between us?

85
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:22,240
And when you said,

86
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:24,240
"So you really don't want me anymore?"

87
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:25,440
Why did you say that?

88
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:31,600
I was just in the mood.

89
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,680
I wanted to see if you'd join in.

90
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,360
Why?

91
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:37,440
You questioned this,

92
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:40,080
but not the money I left you?

93
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,560
Where is the money?

94
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,680
You already took it, didn't you?

95
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:58,600
Why are you like this?

96
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:02,360
You should be glad.

97
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,960
I paid you far more than other women.

98
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:07,160
You know,

99
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:09,400
A used item

100
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:11,400
shouldn't even cost this much.

101
00:10:13,120 --> 00:10:14,560
I've even thrown in an extra.

102
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:19,840
You're not the Song I knew.

103
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,400
The Song you knew?

104
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:25,040
That idiot?

105
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:29,240
I'd never be fooled twice.

106
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:32,960
What?

107
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,040
Wasn't what I gave you enough?

108
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:36,920
Want more?

109
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:40,120
Maybe another round?

110
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:41,760
I can get myself going again.

111
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:53,280
I'm sorry, Ms. Kasira.

112
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:57,120
I thought I had met someone familiar.

113
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:01,160
Sorry for mistaking you for someone else.

114
00:11:04,520 --> 00:11:05,640
I'm truly sorry.

115
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:10,680
♪ But my mouth denies my heart ♪

116
00:11:10,680 --> 00:11:12,560
♪ Never speaking the truth ♪

117
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:17,680
♪ Even though everything I do ♪

118
00:11:17,680 --> 00:11:21,000
♪ Is telling you I love you ♪

119
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:25,000
♪ I give in every time our eyes meet ♪

120
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:33,240
♪ But I'm unable to show it ♪

121
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:40,960
♪ I want to say "I love you" for once,
Just like how I feel ♪

122
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:45,640
Uttawadee,

123
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:47,840
this is only the beginning.

124
00:12:14,240 --> 00:12:19,120
♪ I notice every glance ♪

125
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:23,400
♪ The way you look at me ♪

126
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:28,680
♪ And what they're hiding inside ♪

127
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:33,120
♪ I think we might be the same ♪

128
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:36,640
♪ Hiding our true feelings ♪

129
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:39,880
♪ Not wanting them to come out ♪

130
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:43,160
♪ But the closer we get ♪

131
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:47,120
♪ The more my heart wavers ♪

132
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:51,960
♪ I want to surrender to every voice in my heart ♪

133
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:54,200
♪ But my mouth denies my heart... ♪

134
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:02,640
Ms. Cream!

135
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,560
Mr. Sam is here!

136
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:06,160
Mr. Sam?

137
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:07,200
Yes.

138
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,040
This is for my mother.

139
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:16,280
This is for you and the rest.

140
00:13:24,680 --> 00:13:25,680
Take these too.

141
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:34,880
Mr. Sam.

142
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:35,920
Well,

143
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:37,560
how is my mother?

144
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,600
I'll go see her.

145
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:43,200
What are you doing?

146
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:44,520
Mr. Sam.

147
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,720
We've got a new nurse.

148
00:13:46,720 --> 00:13:48,120
More importantly,

149
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,800
she's Dr. Smith's girlfriend.

150
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,960
No causing trouble this time, okay?

151
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:53,600
Dr. Smith's girlfriend?

152
00:13:54,320 --> 00:13:55,360
Are they planning

153
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:56,320
to move the whole family here?

154
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,040
Mr. Sam!

155
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:58,160
I know!

156
00:14:13,560 --> 00:14:14,560
What is it, Cream?

157
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:16,000
Mr. Sarttra,

158
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,480
Mr. Sam is here.

159
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:20,000
I'll tell Ms. Song first.

160
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,200
"According to English custom,

161
00:14:23,480 --> 00:14:25,760
everyone, noble or commoner,

162
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:28,000
walks into the wedding ceremony

163
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,320
to the same music.

164
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:30,920
The rest of the ceremony

165
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:32,560
is also modeled as closely as possible

166
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:33,560
on the same pattern."

167
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:36,960
Hey, Mom!

168
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:38,560
How have you been?

169
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,360
Here you are, ma'am.

170
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,760
Sam!

171
00:14:58,360 --> 00:14:59,400
Yes, it's me.

172
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:01,560
I missed you so much!

173
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,240
How are you?

174
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:05,240
Did you just get back, dear?

175
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:06,280
Yes.

176
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,920
- Are you hungry?
- Not yet.

177
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,280
Are you tired?

178
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:10,480
Not at all.

179
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:12,920
My, how clingy you are.

180
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:14,840
You're all grown up now.

181
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,920
Grown-ups can be clingy too.

182
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:20,840
Ms. Song,

183
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,640
Cream just called.

184
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:24,120
Mr. Sam is back at the house.

185
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,600
Let him.

186
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:32,240
Sam probably missed Mom too.

187
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:36,120
What's on the schedule today?

188
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:39,240
At 1 p.m.,

189
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:41,080
two event organizers are coming in

190
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,800
to pitch their proposal
for the new collection's launch event.

191
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,160
Would you like to sit in

192
00:15:44,160 --> 00:15:45,200
on the presentation?

193
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,160
I can. I'm not tied up.

194
00:15:48,880 --> 00:15:50,080
So where's the proposal?

195
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,720
Proposal?

196
00:15:51,960 --> 00:15:53,040
Uh,

197
00:15:53,480 --> 00:15:54,440
sure.

198
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,520
I'll go get it for you.

199
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,880
She's going to read the proposal herself?

200
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:41,840
Okay.

201
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,840
Wow!

202
00:16:47,120 --> 00:16:48,080
Here it is.

203
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:49,920
That looks delicious.

204
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:57,600
See, I know exactly what you like, Mom.

205
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,240
Ms. Song.

206
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:13,520
The proposal.

207
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:33,000
Wouldn't it be better

208
00:17:33,880 --> 00:17:35,080
if you went home first?

209
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:37,560
These documents

210
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:39,640
can be signed tomorrow.

211
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,240
What's with you?

212
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:44,440
I'm sitting in on the presentation at 1 p.m.

213
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:45,520
How can I go home first?

214
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:47,880
But Mr. Sam is at the house.

215
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:49,880
So what?

216
00:17:51,320 --> 00:17:52,320
All right.

217
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:39,960
This is number eight.

218
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:41,240
Number eight?

219
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,240
Yes.

220
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:16,440
You're so good, Mom!

221
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:20,240
Are you sleepy now, ma'am?

222
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,080
Yes.

223
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:24,640
How about lying down?

224
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:25,840
Mm-hmm.

225
00:19:25,840 --> 00:19:26,760
Sure.

226
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:30,320
Let me help.

227
00:19:35,480 --> 00:19:36,480
Thanks.

228
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:37,800
I've got it.

229
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,800
Careful, please.

230
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:44,960
All done.

231
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:46,400
Lean back slowly.

232
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:49,000
Okay.

233
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Thanks.

234
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,560
I'll read a book for you.

235
00:19:55,120 --> 00:19:56,040
Sure.

236
00:20:05,640 --> 00:20:06,640
Hello.

237
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:08,800
Yes.

238
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:10,400
I'll have someone come down to get it.

239
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:13,720
Cream, a food delivery is here.

240
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,480
Could you go down and pick it up?

241
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,600
What did you order?

242
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,200
We haven't even finished what you bought.

243
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:19,880
I ordered for Mom, Nueng, Song,

244
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:21,080
and everyone.

245
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:22,920
Hurry down, okay?

246
00:20:23,120 --> 00:20:24,760
The rider's already waiting outside.

247
00:20:26,720 --> 00:20:27,880
Yes, I'll go right now.

248
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,360
I'll go get the book first.

249
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,280
Go on.

250
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:03,360
Mr. Sam.

251
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,120
You can go down and eat first.

252
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:08,880
I'll look after Mom myself.

253
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:10,560
Are you sure?

254
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:13,880
All right then.

255
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:16,120
Oh, let's go down.

256
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:17,440
Mr. Sam ordered so much.

257
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,240
You go ahead, Cream.

258
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:20,760
I'll just tidy up here first.

259
00:21:21,760 --> 00:21:23,200
"According to English custom,

260
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:26,120
everyone, noble or commoner,

261
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:28,760
walks into the wedding ceremony

262
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:30,720
to the same music."

263
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:47,880
Ms. Oh.

264
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:51,280
- Yes?
- Do you have any painkillers?

265
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:53,440
What's wrong, Mr. Sam?

266
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:55,400
I have a headache.

267
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:56,880
It's probably a migraine.

268
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,320
What do you usually take?

269
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:07,600
This one.

270
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:11,080
I think we might have it.

271
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,080
I'll go and check for you.

272
00:22:42,320 --> 00:22:43,440
Did you find it?

273
00:22:44,800 --> 00:22:45,840
No, I didn't.

274
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:48,800
I'll go ask Ms. Cream

275
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:51,000
if we have some in the house.

276
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:55,840
Never mind.

277
00:22:56,320 --> 00:22:57,400
If we don't have that one,

278
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:00,080
there's still something else

279
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:01,440
that can cure a headache.

280
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:02,480
Mr. Sam, let go!

281
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:08,080
What perfume do you wear?

282
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:09,040
You smell so good.

283
00:23:09,280 --> 00:23:10,120
Let me go!

284
00:23:10,120 --> 00:23:11,120
Let go!

285
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:12,520
Let me go!

286
00:23:17,480 --> 00:23:18,480
Oww!

287
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:23,960
You like it rough, huh?

288
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:32,160
Let go!

289
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:45,920
Song!

290
00:23:46,760 --> 00:23:48,400
Did you really have to hit me?

291
00:23:48,600 --> 00:23:49,640
I'll do even more

292
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:51,760
if you don't quit this rotten behavior!

293
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:54,560
Fine.

294
00:23:54,840 --> 00:23:56,360
If you keep taking other people's side

295
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:57,560
